# Iroh, Grand Lotus: "During your turn, each non-Lesson instant and sorcery card in your graveyard has flashback. The
# flashback cost is equal to that card's mana cost. During your turn, each Lesson card in your graveyard has flashback {1}."
# Turn 1: Iroh, then Lightning Bolt at Bot2 (17). Turn 3: Iroh's Demonstration, a sorcery Lesson, from the hand; Iroh
# attacks and firebending 2 adds {R}{R}. In the declare-attackers step Lightning Bolt is offered flashback for {R} (its mana
# cost) and not for {1} (it is no Lesson), and is cast with the firebending mana at Bot2 (14), then exiled (CR 702.34a);
# the Demonstration, a sorcery, may not be flashed back in combat (the ruling: "you must still follow any timing
# restrictions"). Iroh's 5 damage leaves Bot2 at 9. In Bot2's turn 4 the Demonstration has no flashback ("during your
# turn"), with {1} at hand; in Bot1's turn 5 it is cast for {1} - not for its mana cost {1}{R}: a Lesson has only the
# second flashback - and is exiled.

